      "id": "bqu8zlf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Constitutional Amendment"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 368 in Part XX confers power on Parliament to amend the Constitution and lays down the procedure.",
        "An amendment bill can be introduced in either House of Parliament, but cannot be introduced in state legislatures.",
        "Constitutional amendments fall under three categories: Simple Majority, Special Majority under Article 368, and Special Majority with State Ratification.",
        "The Supreme Court established the Basic Structure Doctrine in the Kesavananda Bharati case (1973), limiting Parliament's amending power."
      ],
      "id": "h96q2oo"
    },
