    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "There is NO provision for a joint sitting of both Houses of Parliament in case of a deadlock over a Constitutional Amendment Bill.",
        "Prior permission of the President is NOT required for introducing a Constitutional Amendment Bill.",
        "The President MUST give assent to a Constitutional Amendment Bill after the 24th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1971 made it obligatory."
      ],
      "id": "9osrdo0"
